       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled metformin dose. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, given as 850 mg three times daily. Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, and they give no added glycemic benefit.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1700 mg total daily**, for example 850 mg twice daily\n- **Another dose.** Tell me the intended dose and frequency.\n\nIf you do want 1700 mg three times daily, tell me and add a note on the order with the clinical rationale. I can then enter it as written. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
